WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.479
If you want to hear about what the Wendigo
did in another Stephen King novel after the

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.780
events of Pet Sematary, then stick around
to the end of this video.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.289
Hello and welcome to Horror History, my name
is Professor CZsWorld or whatever the HECK

00:00:15.289 --> 00:00:16.580
you want to call me.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.700
Today’s lesson is about the Wendigo, the
ancient creature that haunts the cursed burial

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.590
ground beyond the Pet Sematary in Ludlow,
Maine.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.980
Stephen King’s Wendigo is based off of an
Algonquian mythological creature, but in the

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.570
novel it is attributed to a different Native
American tribe located near Eastern Canada

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.500
and the northeast United States known as the
Mic-Mac tribe, which is spelled like this

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.260
in the book, probably a reflection of how
Jud Crandall might have pronounced it.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.560
"This was their burial ground."

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.340
"Whose burial ground?"

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.180
"Mic Mac Indians."

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.880
But this is how it’s spelled in real life.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.660
Here are a few pronunciation videos I found.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.670
“Mi’kmaq.”

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.340
OK, so now I know how a robot would pronounce
it.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.960
Let’s try to find the human version.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.080
“Mi’kmaq.”

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.090
“Mic….

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.090
mac....”

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.080
HAHAHA

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.520
So the Wendigo legends told of a huge bipedal
creature, around 15 feet tall.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:06.320
Some versions of the legend tell of a more
human-like form, others skew more beast like,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.161
but all seem to have a few features in common:
they are extremely thin from starvation, to

00:01:10.161 --> 00:01:13.760
the point where you can see their skeleton
poking through the skin all Eugenia Cooney

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.130
style, or even wasting away to the point where
the skeleton is just exposed.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.110
They typically have a stag’s head and antlers,
often have claw-like hands, a wretched smell

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:24.770
of decaying flesh, and patches of fur stained
with human blood.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.990
This is because the legend is told as a metaphor
for greed, consumption and starvation in times

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:33.420
of famine as a way to scare the tribesmen
away from taboo ideas such as cannibalism.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.621
Some versions of the legend tell of humans
who were overtaken by greed turning into Wendigos,

00:01:36.621 --> 00:01:40.990
or in the case of Pet Sematary, those who
came into contact with The Wendigo would become

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:41.990
cannibals.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.640
Let’s explore life of the Wendigo as depicted
in the universe of Stephen King’s novels.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.560
The first mention of the Wendigo dates back
to the pre-1600s when the creature came across

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.740
the Mic-Mac burial ground in Ludlow, Maine.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.390
The Wendigo used it’s demonic powers to
curse the ground, and the tribe soon discovered

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:00.670
that any corpse buried there would be brought
back to life by The Wendigo.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:03.690
Those who have witnessed these reanimated
corpses claim that they can understand some

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.900
truth behind the stereotypical depiction of
a zombie in popular culture, because the corpses

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.340
would come back as a shell of their former
selves, with evil intentions to inflict physical

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.650
and psychological harm to all of those they
come in contact with, including the consumption

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.730
of human flesh.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:21.290
The Mic Mac tribe came to understand this
new, dark power that pulsed throughout their

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.790
resting place and abandoned it some time before
settlers arrived in the 1820s.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:29.540
What I would have done if I were them, is
forget about all this cannibalism stuff change

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.630
my name to the Big Mac tribe and open my own
burger restaurant.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:36.440
Mic Mac Donalds -- and there’s a guy just
up the road who’d love to be the mascot…

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.690
Ludlow became a small agricultural community,
so a main road was established to send crops

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.090
out to be sold on the market.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.510
The Wendigo continued to stalk the woods to
the north of this road, and it’s insatiable

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.890
hunger continued to build.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.801
At the very end of the 1800s and into the
early 1900s, the road became more of a truck

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:55.300
route as automobiles were becoming more prevalent,
which made it a very dangerous place, with

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.970
truckers seeing it as an open stretch of country
road to blow through despite the fact that

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.940
there were families situated on that road.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:04.670
Some say the Wendigo had something to do with
the reckless behavior of these drivers, because

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:09.070
it had some kind of evil influence within
a certain radius of the ground that it soured.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:13.010
Drivers have reported a sudden urge to drive
fast when crossing over into Ludlow and not

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.720
being able to pinpoint why.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.910
This led to an increasing amount of deaths
from pets who had wandered into the road and

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.390
been struck down by these trucks.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.480
For this reason, the kids of the town established
a Pet Sematary in the woods, and I personally

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.920
think it’s no coincidence that this location
 was chosen just shy of the Mic Mac burial ground.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.120
I’d guess that the Wendigo’s influence
manipulated these kids to choose this location.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.620
At some point, someone climbed over the deadfall on the edge of the Pet Sematary, and

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.060
ventured throught the swamp and into the cursed
grounds to bury their pet.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.800
It’s not clear who the first person was
to bury a pet there -- but those who did received

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.680
some kind of curse from the Wendigo, and they’d
almost always end up showing a friend or loved

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.590
one the power the burial ground.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:51.940
The animals who were buried there would be
revived by the Wendigo and come back with

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:55.549
the stink of the ground they were buried in,
and were usually be meaner and more violent

00:03:55.549 --> 00:03:58.310
towards other small animals and sometimes
humans.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:02.220
However, reviving pets who met their fate
too early was not seen as a horrible offense,

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.150
because they lacked the ability to communicate
with humans, so the psychological attacks

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:07.150
were not a factor.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:10.709
It’s just a good thing they didn’t bury
Scooby-Doo, Brian from Family Guy, Garfield,

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:14.510
Stimpy, Courage, Meowth, Detective Pikachu,
Lucy even though he’s not technically a

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:15.510
cat…

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.489
Charlotte from Charlotte’s web, and for
the love of GOD….

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:19.260
The Cat In The Hat.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:26.119
By the time Jud Crandall’s dog Spot died
in 1910, a boy named Stanny B had already

00:04:26.119 --> 00:04:29.110
discovered the burial ground’s secret and
passed it on to Jud.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.169
When Spot was reanimated by the Wendigo and
came back from the dead the next, day, Jud’s

00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:37.300
father was hardly surprised, it seemed that
he too knew of the burial ground’s power,

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.140
although it’s unclear if that was from experience
or if he had just heard about it.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:44.620
He warns his son not to go to the cursed ground
again, and Jud agrees.

00:04:44.639 --> 00:04:49.509
He keeps this promise for a many years, until
one fateful day, when the Wendigo lures Jud

00:04:49.509 --> 00:04:50.640
back to the burial ground.

00:04:57.499 --> 00:05:02.110
Spot lived on another four years after that
and despite a couple small incidents was mostly

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.800
the same, despite being horrifying to Jud’s
mother.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.660
"Jud, come and get your dog!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.280
He stinks of the ground you buried him in!"

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:16.099
But the cycle continued for years, and it
was mostly kept secret by the town’s locals.

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:20.199
At one point a man named Lester Morgan tried
to revive his prized bull Hanratty.

00:05:20.199 --> 00:05:24.160
It is not entirely known how he managed to
lug the massive corpse all the way to the

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.819
burial ground on a sledge, but it is implied
that he received some help from The Wendigo.

00:05:28.819 --> 00:05:32.759
When Hanratty came back, his possession by
the Wendigo was particularly nasty.

00:05:32.759 --> 00:05:36.850
He would charge at anything that moved…
animals, people and even trees swaying in

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.389
the breeze to the point that his horns were
broken and his head was bleeding.

00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:43.930
Lester had to put Hanratty down once again
to spare any additional damage.

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:48.009
The Wendigo continued possessing animals buried
in the place beyond the Pet Sematary until

00:05:48.009 --> 00:05:53.229
1941, where a young Ludlow man named Timmy
Baterman was killed during World War 2.

00:05:53.229 --> 00:05:56.020
Should have stayed home and played Apex Legends
Timmy my man.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.990
His body was sent back to Maine for his funeral,
but his father, stricken with grief, buried

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.520
his body in the Pet Sematary, the first known
human burial since the Mic Mac days.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.180
The Wendigo brought Timmy back, and possessed
him to scare the townsfolk, who all believed

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.429
Timmy was dead.

00:06:09.429 --> 00:06:13.149
People started to notice him walking along
the roadside with a blank look and gossip

00:06:13.149 --> 00:06:16.409
of his return spread faster than a Shane Dawson
conspiracy.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:18.210
OK, maybe not that fast.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.360
Got a little carried away there.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.889
The Wendigo used it’s knowledge of everything
that has happened in the town to torment those

00:06:22.889 --> 00:06:27.029
who he interacted with; divulging their most
embarrassing secrets and making horrible threats

00:06:27.029 --> 00:06:28.479
to some of the women in the town.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:32.729
Timmy’s father ended up going insane from
his undead son’s constant torture, and burned

00:06:32.729 --> 00:06:34.940
down the house with both of them inside.

00:06:34.949 --> 00:06:39.270
The next major incident took place in the
1980s, over 70 years since Jud buried his

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:40.809
dog Spot for the first time.

00:06:40.809 --> 00:06:44.089
Jud had just befriended the Creed family,
who had just moved in across the street from

00:06:44.089 --> 00:06:45.089
him.

00:06:45.089 --> 00:06:48.360
When the family’s cat was run down in the
road, Jud took Louis Creed to bury the cat

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.120
in the Mic Mac burial ground, finally breaking
the promise to his father that he would not

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.120
go back there.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:57.189
Jud believed that he never meant to show Louis
the cursed place, that the power of The Wendigo

00:06:57.189 --> 00:07:01.460
made him do it, and by introducing Louis to
the soured grounds, he transferred the curse

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.959
to Louis’s family.

00:07:02.959 --> 00:07:07.360
Not long after, the young boy Gage ran into
the street and was killed, and I mean freaking

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.900
YEETed by an oncoming truck, a tragedy that
Jud felt he was partially responsible for

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.580
because he showed Louis the burial ground.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.470
The Wendigo has the ability to influence those
within a certain radius of the cursed ground

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:22.650
and for the next two days, it constantly puts
ideas about digging up Gage and putting him

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.919
in the Mic Mac grounds into Louis’s head.

00:07:24.919 --> 00:07:28.929
Louis sends his remaining family away to visit
his wife’s parents in Chicago, claiming

00:07:28.929 --> 00:07:31.740
he needs to wrap some things up at work before
joining them.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.669
This gives him the privacy he needs to retrieve
his son and take him up past the Pet Sematary

00:07:35.669 --> 00:07:38.399
and over the deadfall towards the forbidden
burying ground.

00:07:38.399 --> 00:07:42.379
His wife, Rachel, senses something is wrong
and travels back to Maine on a string of last

00:07:42.379 --> 00:07:46.550
second flights, but after just missing the
last flight, she’s unable to get there on

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:47.550
time.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:50.509
She talks on the phone with Jud, who realizes
what is happening and tries to stay up and

00:07:50.509 --> 00:07:54.430
wait out for Louis, hoping to talk him out
of this despicable act.

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:58.169
Despite not being tired at first, Jud quickly
starts to doze off and recognizes that the

00:07:58.169 --> 00:08:02.219
Wendigo is doing this to him to try to clear
any obstacles in Louis’s path.

00:08:02.219 --> 00:08:07.279
Jud does everything he can to stay awake,
but in the end passes out before Louis arrives.

00:08:07.279 --> 00:08:11.379
As Louis approaches the cemetery, the fog
around him goes into a swirl and encloses

00:08:11.379 --> 00:08:12.379
him.

00:08:12.379 --> 00:08:14.860
He feels that the swamp around him is alive
and sentient.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.560
When the mist clears, Louis sees a pair of
yellow-grey eyes before him.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:23.180
A spirit with rotting teeth, the curved horns
of a ram, and peeling flesh, was laughing

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.759
in the distance before him.

00:08:24.759 --> 00:08:29.439
As Louis trudged on after that, the face floated
before him at a constant distance, until it

00:08:29.439 --> 00:08:31.880
eventually faded back into the mist.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:37.020
The frogs and insects of the swamp go quiet
as a huge creature shakes the ground with

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.740
it’s footsteps and approaches Louis.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:42.550
A vile smell fills the air as the monster
gets closer to him.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:46.630
As it reaches its closest point, Louis looks
up and sees the sparks of a pair of yellowish

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.130
eyes some sixty feet above him.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:53.550
The Wendigo, knowing Louis is heading to the
Mic Mac grounds, lets Louis pass as it continues

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:54.579
going north.

00:08:54.579 --> 00:08:58.870
As Louis continues, he comes across a massive
claw-like footprint and forces himself to

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:02.310
believe that it was something else to keep
himself from going insane.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.550
Louis buries his son in the cursed burial
ground, goes home and goes to bed.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:10.459
During the night, The Wendigo goes ahead and
revives Gage, who kills both Jud Crandall

00:09:10.459 --> 00:09:11.790
and Rachel.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:15.579
Louis discovers their bodies in the morning
and goes crazy after seeing what the monster

00:09:15.579 --> 00:09:20.470
has done to his wife, but the last sane thought
that crosses through his mind, is the image

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:23.750
of the Wendigo in the swamp that previous
night.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.500
As he heads up the forest path with Rachel’s
body, Louis’s physician’s assistant Steve

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:31.680
Masterton sees him disappear over the deadfall,
presumably passing on the knowledge of the

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:36.790
burial ground once again to feed the Wendigo’s
insatiable hunger with a new set of victims.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:41.759
It’s unknown what happened to the Wendigo
from then until almost 15 years later, in

00:09:41.759 --> 00:09:43.100
the summer of 1997.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:46.800
Actually, it’s not really confirmed that
The Wendigo comes back at all, but there are

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.700
many people who believe that an evil deity
from Stephen King’s novel The Girl Who Loved

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:53.950
Tom Gordon, is in fact, the Wendigo from Pet
Sematary.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.040
I don’t personally think there’s enough
evidence to draw this conclusion, but there

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.160
are some points that I find interesting anyways.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:02.970
The story is about a 9 year old girl named
Patricia McFarland who goes missing while

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:06.560
hiking with her Mom and her brother on the
Appalachian Trail in Eastern Maine.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.240
The area she first gets lost in isn’t very
close to the woods that The Wendigo prowled

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.860
in Pet Sematary, but if you continue down
the Appalachian Trail, it does continue to

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.399
go toward Ludlow, so it’s possible that
the Wendigo traveled this stretch of woods

00:10:17.399 --> 00:10:19.190
after destroying Louis Creed’s family.

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:23.010
After getting separated from her family and
lost from the path, Trisha continues down

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:27.319
along a stream to try to find civilization,
and she notices some disturbing signs along

00:10:27.319 --> 00:10:31.870
the way, like a tree that has been slashed
at by some giant claws and a decapitated deer,

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.959
which is maybe the strongest evidence towards
this creature actually being the Wendigo,

00:10:34.959 --> 00:10:38.300
considering that Wendigo are most often depicted
with a stag’s head.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:41.850
The further into her journey she gets, the
more the voice in her head tells her that

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:45.589
this “thing” is following her, At some
point, as Trish starts to hallucinate some

00:10:45.589 --> 00:10:49.540
strange images and it’s not entirely clear
what’s real and what’s in her mind.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:54.079
She comes across a trio of robed figures in
the form of her history teacher, her father,

00:10:54.079 --> 00:10:58.019
and the God of the Lost, the creature that
has supposedly been following and watching

00:10:58.019 --> 00:10:59.019
her.

00:10:59.019 --> 00:11:02.290
It’s head appears to her in the form of
one of her fears during the journey, a swarm

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:03.290
of wasps.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:06.870
After several days she finally makes it out
of the wilderness to a road, and the God of

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.950
the Lost comes for her in the form of a bear
like creature, but she and the hunter who

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:15.029
helps her scare off the deity, are never quite
convinced this is an actual bear and both

00:11:15.029 --> 00:11:17.769
seem to have the idea in their heads that
it’s actually something supernatural.

00:11:17.769 --> 00:11:22.360
It could be the Wendigo, or it could be some
wild creature that was revived by the Wendigo

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.040
and is now being controlled by it.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:27.180
Personally, I just don’t see a lot of strong
connections between the two, and I’d have

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:30.129
to say they are maybe related entities at
best.

00:11:30.129 --> 00:11:34.110
Just as the Wendigo in Algonquian folklore
was used to warn against taboo behaviours

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:38.110
such as cannibalism, the Wendigo in Stephen
King’s stories warns against tampering with

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.760
the natural order of life.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:44.269
In Pet Sematary, the Wendigo tempts a doctor
who has lost his son to defy nature to bring

00:11:44.269 --> 00:11:48.170
him back after being unable to resuscitate
one of his patients earlier in the story.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:52.290
In this sense it’s very similar to the classic
horror story Frankenstein, because in trying

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.279
to create life, this doctor ends up creating
a monster.

00:11:55.279 --> 00:11:59.610
The Wendigo represents the taboo; that line
that should never be crossed by any man.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:03.760
It is an evil force and an embodiment of those
things that go against nature.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.681
The Girl Who Loved Tom Gordon also contains
themes of man vs nature… or at least 9 year

00:12:08.681 --> 00:12:13.079
old girl vs nature… but they are conveyed
in a much more positive way, with Trisha “defying

00:12:13.079 --> 00:12:16.720
nature” by overcoming seemingly impossible
odds to survive.

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.879
So that wraps up today’s lesson here on
Horror History.

00:12:19.879 --> 00:12:23.680
Your homework is to like this video and let
me know what your thoughts are on The Wendigo

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.680
and The God of the Lost in the comments.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:26.680
Are they the same?

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:27.740
Are they related?

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.930
Or are there other similar themes that tie
them together?

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.870
I’ll be looking forward to your responses.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:36.920
Check out the video on the left for 47 Things
